 ## Overview
-This method converts a greedy mesh quad into four vertex indices packed into u32, applying ambient occlusion (AO) blending and correcting for interpolation anisotropy [S1, S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem where vertex-based AO values create visible seams or inconsistent shading gradients across a quad face due to the arbitrary direction of the splitting diagonal [S2, unofficial]. It differs from its parent [Binary Greedy Voxel Meshing with Ambient Occlusion](4465-binary-greedy-voxel-meshing-with-ambient-occlusion.md) by actively rotating the vertex order to ensure the diagonal connects vertices with higher combined occlusion, thereby smoothing the gradient [S2, unofficial].
